  <h2>What is TWRP?</h2>
  <p>
    Team Win Recovery Project is an open-source custom recovery maintained by Team
    Win. A recovery is a small bootable environment that lives apart from Android
    itself: the stock one can apply system updates and factory-reset the phone.
    TWRP replaces it with a touch-driven environment that can flash ZIP packages,
    create and restore full partition backups (Nandroid), and mount, format, or
    wipe individual partitions.
  </p>

  <h2>Builds are device-specific</h2>
  <p>
    TWRP is built per device model, and only a build made for your exact model is
    safe to use — the official site's Devices section lists every supported model.
    Installing a custom recovery also generally requires an unlocked bootloader,
    which factory-resets the device on most phones.
  </p>

  <h2>Know before you flash</h2>
